✅ ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤
   │ npm start     │ Start dev server with proxy │
   ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤
   │ npm run build │ Build for production        │
   ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤
   │ npm test      │ Run unit tests              │
   ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤
   │ npm run watch │ Build in watch mode (dev)   │
   └───────────────┴─────────────────────────────┘


  1. Open a terminal (PowerShell or Command Prompt)

  2. Navigate to the project folder:
  cd C:\Users\Ranjith\Downloads\files-rag\rag-frontend-angular\rag-frontend

  3. Install dependencies (only needed once):
  npm install

  4. Start the dev server:
  npm start

  or equivalently:



npm npm
   The app uses a proxy config (proxy.conf.json) which likely forwards API calls to your backend. Make sure your backend is also running if the app makes API
   requests.n